  "body": "## What changed\n`web/build-app-wasm.sh`: `sed_in_place` returns 1 (naming the file) when sed or the move fails, instead of relying on an `&&` list that bash exempts from `set -e`. Its three callers now stop the script with `die \"cannot patch <file>\"`. Successful runs are unchanged.\n\n## How tested\n- `bash -n web/build-app-wasm.sh` passes.\n- Scratch-dir test outside the repo, with a fake failing `sed` on PATH: helper returns 1 and prints `sed failed on <file>`, no `.tmp` left behind; a caller with `|| die` stops the script; the success path still replaces the file.\n- Pinning test: none (a shell script has no test harness in the gate).\n\n## Not exercised\n- Not run on macOS / bash 3.2.\n- The wasm build was not executed.\n\nChangelog: none (build script fix, no user-visible behaviour change)\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #1486\n",
